<title>UK: Facts &amp; figures in the UK/US telecoms markets.</title>
<headline>Facts &amp; figures in the UK/US telecoms markets.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission on Wednesday blessed the $20 billion merger between British Telecommunications Plc and MCI Communications Corp leaving U.S. regulatory clearance the deal's last hurdle.</p>
<p>BT expects to win U.S. approval by autumn. But a green light hinges on whether the British market is deemed to be as open to U.S. players as the American market is to British ones.</p>
<p>The folowing is a table of key facts and figures that affect the British and American telecommunications markets, according to data provided by BT.</p>
<p>					    US		    UK</p>
<p>TOTAL POPULATION:		   267 million		59 million</p>
<p>PHONE LINES PER 100 PEOPLE:	62.7		  47</p>
<p>INDUSTRY VALUE:	    US			    UK</p>
<p>				     (figures in stg)</p>
<p>  Total:	     150   bln			18   bln</p>
<p>  Local:		60   bln   Domestic:	 8.1 bln</p>
<p>  Long Distance:    45   bln   International:  2.6 bln</p>
<p>  Wireless:	   12.6 bln   Leased lines:   1.2 bln</p>
<p>  Internet:	    4.2 bln   Data:	     2.1 bln</p>
<p>  SI/Net management 28   bln   Wireless:	 3   bln</p>
<p>					 Other:	    0.8 bln</p>
<p>TOP 10 TELECOM GROUPS (BY REVENUE):</p>
<p>	    US				UK</p>
<p>1:AT &amp; T Corp	   British Telecommunications</p>
<p>2:GTE Corp	    Mercury</p>
<p>3:BellSouth Corp    Vodafone Group Plc</p>
<p>4:MCI			     Cellnet</p>
<p>5:Bell Atlantic Corp Orange Plc</p>
<p>6:Ameritech Corp     One2One</p>
<p>7:NYNEX Corp	  Kingston Communications</p>
<p>8:Sprint Corp	 Telewest</p>
<p>9:SBC Communications COLT</p>
<p>10:US West Inc	NYNEX CableComms</p>
<p>NUMBER OF TELECOM PROVIDERS:</p>
